As founder of Grabaciones Los Poderosos (which loosely translates to &#8220;powerful recordings&#8221;), Feid (real name: Salomón Villada Hoyos) will have full ownership of his masters, ensuring creative autonomy and long-term control of his catalog, as well as establishing a structure in support of his future releases.&nbsp;

Billboard can also confirm that the artist&#8217;s new business model and label structure will cover different areas of entertainment, including management, touring, booking, marketing and audiovisual services.

“For now, my focus is on taking my project to the next level, growing my label and continuing to push my music forward,” he shares. “I’m really excited and grateful to finally share the news of Grabaciones Los Poderosos with you all.”

Feid’s first Billboard chart entry arrived in 2016 with the J Balvin-featuring “Que Raro,” debuting and peaking at No. 26 on Latin Digital Song Sales and peaking at No. 16 on Latin Rhythm Airplay. Since then, he’s earned eight Top 10 hits on Hot Latin Songs, seven songs in the all-genre Billboard Hot 100, and 12 No. 1s in Latin Airplay, including “Hablame Claro” with Yandel, “Verano Rosa” with Karol G, and &#8220;Se Lo Juro Mor,&#8221;—all which crowned the chart in 2025.&nbsp;

